IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XVI, ss 193 and 194: GOING-PRIVATE
-- TRANSACTIONS AND SQUEEZE-OUT TRANSACTIONS. Sections 195 to 205 are repealed in this text.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. A "going-private transaction" is one the regulations define (s 2(1) points there; the
-- regulations are not among the sources). A "squeeze-out transaction" is defined in s 2(1) (the keel's
-- rule). Section 193 lets a corporation carry out the first, subject to provincial securities laws; section
-- 194 lets it carry out the second only with the approval of each affected class, voting separately.
--
-- Whether a transaction IS a going-private or squeeze-out transaction is the keel's question
-- (`squeeze-out transaction within s 2(1)`, and a plain input for the going-private definition). These
-- rules take the answer as a fact.

§§ `s 193 Going-private transactions`

-- src:2485 | PART XVI Going-private Transactions and Squeeze-out Transactions
-- src:2486 | Going-private transactions
-- src:2487 | 193 A corporation may carry out a going-private transaction. However, if there are any applicable provincial securities laws, a corporation may not carry out a going-private transaction unless the corporation complies with those laws.
@ref CBCA s 193 (src:2487)
GIVEN `there are applicable provincial securities laws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation complies with those laws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a corporation may carry out a going-private transaction within s 193` MEANS
        (NOT `there are applicable provincial securities laws`)
    OR  `the corporation complies with those laws`

§§ `s 194 Squeeze-out transactions`

-- "Voting separately, whether or not the shares otherwise carry the right to vote": the right to vote is
-- given on every share of an affected class; but two groups "do not have the right to vote on the
-- resolution": affiliates of the corporation, and holders who would get consideration of greater value or
-- superior rights or privileges than the other holders of the same class.
-- src:2488 | Squeeze-out transactions
-- src:2489 | 194 A corporation may not carry out a squeeze-out transaction unless, in addition to any approval by holders of shares required by or under this Act or the articles of the corporation, the transaction is approved by ordinary resolution of the holders of each class of shares that are affected by the transaction, voting separately, whether or not the shares otherwise carry the right to vote. However, the following do not have the right to vote on the resolution:
-- src:2490 | (a) affiliates of the corporation; and
-- src:2491 | (b) holders of shares that would, following the squeeze-out transaction, be entitled to consideration of greater value or to superior rights or privileges than those available to other holders of shares of the same class.
@ref CBCA s 194 (src:2489-2491)
GIVEN `the shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder is an affiliate of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder would be entitled after the transaction to consideration of greater value or to superior rights or privileges than other holders of the same class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holder may vote on the squeeze-out resolution within s 194` MEANS
        (NOT `the holder is an affiliate of the corporation`)
    AND (NOT `the holder would be entitled after the transaction to consideration of greater value or to superior rights or privileges than other holders of the same class`)

-- The holders of one affected class have approved by ordinary resolution, counting the votes of those
-- entitled to vote on it.
@ref CBCA s 194 (src:2489)
GIVEN tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holders of a class have approved the squeeze-out transaction within s 194` MEANS
    `ordinary resolution within s 2(1)` tally

-- Not "may not unless": for a transaction that is not a squeeze-out transaction, section 194 sets no
-- condition (NOTHING), which is different from "may not".
@ref CBCA s 194 (src:2489)
GIVEN `the transaction is a squeeze-out transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approvals required by or under this Act or the articles have been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every class of shares affected has approved by ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the corporation may carry out the squeeze-out transaction within s 194` MEANS
    IF `the transaction is a squeeze-out transaction`
    THEN JUST (    `the approvals required by or under this Act or the articles have been obtained`
               AND `every class of shares affected has approved by ordinary resolution`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 195 to 205`

-- Repealed in this text: "195 to 205 [Repealed, 2001, c. 14, s. 97]" (src:2492). There is nothing to encode.
